  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "REQ-BEHAVIOR",
      "classification": "normative",
      "status": "mapped",
      "mapping_kind": "both",
      "text": "Implement benchmark_dot, a 2-lane signed INT8 dot product with a signed 32-bit sum.\nLane i uses packed bits [8*i +: 8] of req_a/req_b. Each product and the complete\nsum are exact; sign-extend the result. Accept only when req_valid && req_ready.\nSingle outstanding request; req_ready stays low while busy. A request accepted\nat edge t produces rsp_valid immediately after edge t+2 (three rising edges\ncounting the accepting edge). Hold rsp_valid/rsp_data until response handshake.\nreq_ready is high again AFTER a response-accepting edge; no same-edge bypass.\nActive-low asynchronous reset or synchronous kill clears the outstanding work,\nrsp_data=0, and returns to idle; kill immediately masks req_ready/rsp_valid.\nNo response from cancelled work. Inputs may change while busy. Mask ready/valid\nwhile reset is low; rsp_data starts/reset-clears to zero and otherwise holds.",
      "evidence": [
        "task.md"
      ],
